  "fullContentHtml": "\n<h1 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-e52a0102 gb-headline-text\">Bihar Vidhan Parishad Security Guard Interview Admit Card 2026</h1>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-659bd175\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-a344b6f7\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-31d42cf5\">\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-c57ae0af gb-headline-text\">Post Date: <time class=\"entry-date published\" datetime=\"2026-06-09T11:36:55+05:30\">June 9, 2026</time></p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<span class=\"custom-post-time\">11:36 am</span>\n\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-550ae316 short_Details gb-headline-text\"></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Bihar Vidhan Parishad,</strong> has release the<strong> Interview Admit Card</strong>&nbsp;on its&nbsp;<strong>official website</strong> for the <strong>Reporter, Assistant, Assistant Caretaker, Data Entry Operator (DEO), Lower Division Clerk (LDC), Security Guard, Driver and Office Attendant Examination 2024.</strong> The <b>Interview</b>&nbsp;<span data-teams=\"true\">will be conducted on<strong> June 2026</strong></span><strong>,</strong>&nbsp;The&nbsp;<strong>Bihar Vidhan Parishad</strong>&nbsp;application process started on&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"319\" data-end=\"339\">16 October 2024</strong>, and candidates were able to submit their applications until&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"401\" data-end=\"424\">25 October 2024</strong>. Candidates can check their <strong>Interview Admit Card</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>using their&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"302\" data-end=\"362\">Enrollment Number, Registration Number, or Date of Birth</strong>&nbsp;by logging into the portal. The direct link is provided below.&nbsp;<span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>(Advt. No: 01/2023, 02/2023, 03/2023 &amp; 04/2023)</strong></span></span></p>\n<p></p>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-9849916c\">\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p></p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.vinod.sarkarinaukri&amp;hl=en_IN\" class=\"apply-button\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        Download SarkariResult App Now\n    </a>\n    </div>\n    \n<div class=\"social-buttons\"><!-- WhatsApp Button --> <a class=\"social-button whatsapp\" href=\"https://whatsapp.com/channel/0029VaAbQf01NCrYADMLt00L\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> WhatsApp </a> <!-- Telegram Button --> <a class=\"social-button telegram\" href=\"https://t.me/SarkariExam_info\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> Telegram </a></div>\n\n\n\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-f58e6ca1\">\n\n<h2 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-2ca5a791 gb-headline-text\">Bihar Vidhan Parishad Security Guard Interview Admit Card 2026</h2>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-7d5f86e8 gb-headline-text\">Bihar Vidhan Parishad Various Post Examination 2023 : Short Details</h3>\n\n<p class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-79adf169 gb-headline-text\"><a href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/bihar-vidhan-parishad-security-guard-2026/\">SarkariResult.com.cm</a></p>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-wrapper gb-grid-wrapper-303102a8\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-d96c68be\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-d96c68be\">\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-16a90584\">\n\n<h4 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-22b2e02b gb-headline-text\"><strong>Important Dates</strong></h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-3b2f0e17 gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Online Apply Start Date : <strong>25 July 2023</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Online Apply Last Date : <strong>21 August 2023</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Last Date For Fee Payment : <b>21 August 2023</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Online Apply <span style=\"background-color: #ffff00;\"><strong>Re-Open</strong></span> Start Date : <b>16 October 2024</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Online Apply Last Date : <strong>25 October 2024</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Fee Payment Last Date :&nbsp;<strong>25 October 2024</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Interview Date : <b>08 – 22 January 2024</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Security Guard Admit Card :&nbsp;<b>18-26 September 2025</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Physical Exam Date :<strong>&nbsp;21-28 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Physical Admit Card:&nbsp;<b>15 April 2026</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">PET Result : <strong>21 May 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Interview Admit Card : <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>08 June 2026 Available Now</strong></span></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates are advised to confirm from the <b>Bihar Vidhan Sabha </b>official website.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-fcbb81ff\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-fcbb81ff\">\n\n<h4 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-4ddaf9ee gb-headline-text\"><strong>Application Fee</strong></h4>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-989f3ffd gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">For <strong>Other Category Candidates</strong> :<strong> ₹ 1200/-</strong></span></li>\n<li>For <strong>SC/ ST/ All Female/ PwD : ₹<span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">&nbsp;600/-</span></strong></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Payment Mode (Online):</strong> You can make the payment using the following methods:</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Debit Card</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Credit Card</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Internet Banking</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">IMPS</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Cash Card / Mobile Wallet</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-6b6fbcac\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-wrapper gb-grid-wrapper-8aa46b64\">\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-0f18d865\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-0f18d865\">\n<h5 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-0b3ada47 gb-headline-text\">Bihar Vidhan Parishad Various Post Notification 2023 : Age Limits As On 01 January 2023.</h5>\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-28dede61 gb-headline-text\"><ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Minimum Age : <strong>18 – 21 Year (Post Wise)</strong></span></li>\n<li>\n<div><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Maximum Age : <strong>37 Years</strong></span></div>\n</li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><b>Bihar Vidhan Parishad </b>provides age relaxation for the&nbsp;<strong>Various positions</strong>&nbsp;as per their regulations.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n<div class=\"gb-grid-column gb-grid-column-860b2712\"><div class=\"gb-container gb-container-860b2712\">\n\n<h5 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-f2184b83 gb-headline-text\"><strong>Total Post</strong></h5>\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-4259c0c2 gb-headline-text\">176 Posts</div>\n</div></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<!-- SarkariResult -->\n\n\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\">\n<a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.vinod.sarkarinaukri&amp;hl=en_IN\" class=\"apply-button\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        Download SarkariResult App Now\n    </a>\n    </div>\n    \n\n</div>\n\n\n\n<!-- SarkariResult -->\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"gb-container gb-container-ec1f6e4c\">\n<h6 class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-c7683bda gb-headline-text\">Bihar Vidhan Parishad Various Post Recruitment 2023 : Vacancy Details</h6>\n\n<div class=\"gb-headline gb-headline-60ccea19 gb-headline-text\"><table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>No. Of Post</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Reporter</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">16</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Assistant</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">30</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Assistant Caretaker</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">01</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Data Entry Operator (DEO)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">40</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Lower Division Clerk (LDC)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">09</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Security Guard</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">56</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Driver</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">04</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">06</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Watchman)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">01</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Faras)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">06</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Sweeper)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">03</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Mali)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 50%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">04</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9542%; height: 1512px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Post Name</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 204px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 204px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Reporter</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 204px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a <strong>Bachelor’s degree</strong> from a university recognized by the State or Central Government. They should have <strong>Hindi stenography speed of 150 words per minute</strong> and <strong>typing speed of 35 words per minute in both Hindi and English</strong>. Additionally, candidates must possess a <strong>computer certificate</strong> recognized by AICTE or DOEACC/NIELIT (equivalent to ‘O’ Level), or must have passed a <strong>Computer Proficiency Test</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 153px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 153px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Assistant</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 153px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a <strong>Bachelor’s degree</strong> from a State or Central Government recognized university. They should have a <strong>typing speed of 30 words per minute in both Hindi and English</strong> and must also possess a <strong>computer course certificate</strong> from AICTE, DOEACC, or NIELIT.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 76px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 76px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Assistant Caretaker</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 76px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have a <strong>Bachelor’s degree</strong> from a university recognized by the State or Central Government.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 127px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Data Entry Operator (DEO)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Intermediate (10+2)</strong> from a recognized board or council of the State or Central Government. They should also have a <strong>typing speed of 8000 key depressions per hour (KDPH) on computer</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 127px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Lower Division Clerk (LDC)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Intermediate (10+2)</strong> from a recognized board or council of the State or Central Government. They should also have a <strong>typing speed of 30 words per minute in both Hindi and English</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 357px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 357px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Security Guard</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 357px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Intermediate (10+2)</strong> in any subject from a recognized board or council of the State or Central Government. For physical standards, male candidates should have a height of <strong>167.5 cm</strong> (relaxation of 2.4 cm for Terai region), chest <strong>76.5–81 cm</strong>, and vision <strong>6/12 without glasses</strong>. Female candidates should have a height of <strong>154.6 cm</strong> (with similar relaxation for Terai region) and vision <strong>6/12 without glasses</strong>. Candidates must be <strong>physically fit and free from diseases</strong>. Additionally, male candidates must complete a <strong>1.6 km run in 6 minutes</strong>, and female candidates must complete a <strong>1 km run in 6 minutes</strong>. Preference will be given to candidates with an <strong>NCC ‘C’ certificate</strong> or those who have represented the state, country, or university in sports at a recognized level.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 102px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 102px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Driver</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 102px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>10th (Matriculation)</strong> from a recognized board in India and must possess a <strong>valid driving license (LMV/HMV)</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 127px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Matric (10th) or equivalent</strong> from a recognized board. They should have a <strong>working knowledge of both Hindi and English languages</strong> and must also know how to <strong>ride a bicycle</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 127px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Watchman)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 127px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Matric (10th) or equivalent</strong> from a recognized board. They should have a <strong>working knowledge of both Hindi and English languages</strong> and must also have the <strong>ability to ride a bicycle</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Faras)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Matric (10th) or equivalent</strong> from a recognized board. They should have a <strong>working knowledge of both Hindi and English languages</strong> and must also have the <strong>ability to ride a bicycle</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Sweeper)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Matric (10th) or equivalent</strong> from a recognized board. They should have a <strong>working knowledge of both Hindi and English languages</strong> and must also have the <strong>ability to ride a bicycle</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 28px;\">\n<td style=\"width: 26.3473%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Office Attendant (Mali)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 167.767%; text-align: center; height: 28px;\">\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Candidates must have passed <strong>Matric (10th) or equivalent</strong> from a recognized board. They should have a <strong>working knowledge of both Hindi and English languages</strong> and must also have the <strong>ability to ride a bicycle</strong>.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #800000;\">You May Also Check : </span></strong><strong><a href=\"https://sarkariresult.com.cm/dsssb-non-teaching-various-post-recruitment-2025/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DSSSB Non-Teaching Various Post Online Form 2025</a></strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"background-color: #000080; color: #ffffff; font-size: 14pt;\"><strong>&nbsp;How To Check &amp; Download Bihar Vidhan Parishad Security Guard Interview Admit Card 2026&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td styl